  "transcript": [
    {
      "start": 6.0,
      "end": 11.76,
      "text": "On 275 and 285. Also in stereo on VHF. This is National Radio 1.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 11.76,
      "end": 27.87,
      "text": "This is TV on the Radio here, Thomas the Vance, and welcome once again to The Friday Rock Show.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 27.87,
      "end": 40.87,
      "text": "Okay, tonight two superb sessions for your aural delight. Out of the archives, recorded in 1976 by four great musicians, we have Brand X, plus five new versions of Gillan tracks, recorded just a fortnight ago.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 40.87,
      "end": 59.28,
      "text": "on top of that i've got some new releases by nightwing queen savage iron maiden and the band",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 59.28,
      "end": 65.08,
      "text": "called alcatraz some classic cuts by lord such and heavy friends and others that you'll find in",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 65.08,
      "end": 69.94,
      "text": "the friday night connection we have the answer to last week's plus a brand new one but tonight",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 69.94,
      "end": 81.34,
      "text": "we start with this from a brand new album that's just come out on the career record label it's",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 81.34,
      "end": 355.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 360.0,
      "end": 618.04,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 616.7,
      "end": 620.62,
      "text": "called the eagle has landed obviously i don't have to tell you it's the new album by saxon",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 620.94,
      "end": 622.52,
      "text": "It's absolutely impeccable.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 623.04,
      "end": 626.84,
      "text": "The Traxie Herber Princess of the Night and 747 Strangers in the Night.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 627.8,
      "end": 632.24,
      "text": "Dedicate all that to Bob Porter, who's a gentleman who was 18 years of age on May the 4th.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 632.48,
      "end": 633.9,
      "text": "He lives in Hartley-Whitney in Hampshire.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 634.44,
      "end": 638.54,
      "text": "And he says, P.S. I don't know why people get so excited about 18th birthdays.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 639.14,
      "end": 642.92,
      "text": "It's only the time when you can do legally what you've been doing illegally for years.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 643.42,
      "end": 644.12,
      "text": "Naughty fella.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 645.41,
      "end": 648.49,
      "text": "Also, I'd like to say hello to a gentleman who is married to Jill.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 648.81,
      "end": 650.97,
      "text": "Jill Cannon, that is, of 13 Holly Rise,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 651.53,
      "end": 653.25,
      "text": "New Allerton, Newark in Nottinghamshire.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 653.39,
      "end": 654.85,
      "text": "He had a birthday, actually, today.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 655.21,
      "end": 656.25,
      "text": "Happy birthday from the message.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 658.14,
      "end": 659.74,
      "text": "And finally, this little card says,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 659.82,
      "end": 661.34,
      "text": "Dear Tom, please say hi to the headbangers,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 661.46,
      "end": 662.68,
      "text": "Steve, Tony, Jack and Simon,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 662.78,
      "end": 664.44,
      "text": "not to mention Andy, John and Ivo,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 664.78,
      "end": 666.38,
      "text": "and play something by Rush for them.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 666.46,
      "end": 667.78,
      "text": "Not this week, but maybe next.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 668.3,
      "end": 671.5,
      "text": "It's now 14 after 10.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 671.56,
      "end": 673.74,
      "text": "This is the Friday Rock Show from BBC Radio 1.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 673.74,
      "end": 675.7,
      "text": "It's a pleasure now to introduce Gillan.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 676.24,
      "end": 679.84,
      "text": "They toured with Gillan during 1981.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 679.84,
      "end": 1272.02,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1272.76,
      "end": 1273.76,
      "text": "They're called Nightwing.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1273.76,
      "end": 1275.88,
      "text": "Their album is out on the Gold Record label.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1276.02,
      "end": 1276.88,
      "text": "It's called Black Summer.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1277.02,
      "end": 1278.56,
      "text": "The track was Long Hard Road.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1279.5,
      "end": 1283.01,
      "text": "Did so well on that tour,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1283.11,
      "end": 1285.03,
      "text": "they're going to be doing their own headline tour",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1285.03,
      "end": 1287.61,
      "text": "during this year over there in Germany.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1287.73,
      "end": 1289.93,
      "text": "They're doing 25 gigs, including one support",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1289.93,
      "end": 1292.37,
      "text": "when they support a master called Zapper.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1292.91,
      "end": 1295.19,
      "text": "And before that, the first of five that we've got tonight",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1295.19,
      "end": 1298.85,
      "text": "from our recently recorded session by Ian Gillan and his cronies.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1298.95,
      "end": 1300.19,
      "text": "The track was called Vengeance.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1300.91,
      "end": 1305.52,
      "text": "All that was for a fellow by the name of John Sibley,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1305.52,
      "end": 1308.12,
      "text": "who was 30 years of age on Tuesday.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1309.08,
      "end": 1311.62,
      "text": "Lots of love from Claire of Tamworth and Staffordshire.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1314.9,
      "end": 1316.82,
      "text": "And Sid needs a mention.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1317.06,
      "end": 1319.48,
      "text": "Sid lives in, I think, in and around Manchester somewhere.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1320.48,
      "end": 1321.68,
      "text": "It's, er...",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1321.68,
      "end": 1323.06,
      "text": "Well, I think it's his birthday today.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1323.24,
      "end": 1324.96,
      "text": "Well, if it isn't, happy whatever.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1325.14,
      "end": 1326.66,
      "text": "Happy Friday from Francis Dean.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1327.82,
      "end": 1329.3,
      "text": "And here's a little card from Robbie Wilson,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1329.46,
      "end": 1331.04,
      "text": "who wants me to say hello to Alan and Kenny",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1331.04,
      "end": 1333.88,
      "text": "and Alan and Mark and Davey, who are new blood.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1334.38,
      "end": 1336.4,
      "text": "And also Jim, Gavin, Margaret, Andrew, Stuart,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1336.66,
      "end": 1337.54,
      "text": "Colleen, I think it is.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1337.54,
      "end": 1340.98,
      "text": "and all the others doing O Grades and Hires at Stranraer Academy.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1341.52,
      "end": 1343.46,
      "text": "And also hello to Marilyn and Phil.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1343.46,
      "end": 1347.41,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1348.67,
      "end": 1352.09,
      "text": "We're together in the BBC studios in February of 1976.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1352.41,
      "end": 1353.15,
      "text": "Brand X.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1353.15,
      "end": 2112.79,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 2112.79,
      "end": 2115.07,
      "text": "MAD, Mutually Assured Destruction.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2115.17,
      "end": 2117.59,
      "text": "That was put together by Gillan about a fortnight ago.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2118.33,
      "end": 2119.39,
      "text": "Magnificent piece of music.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2119.53,
      "end": 2122.37,
      "text": "Before that, out of the archives from 1976, Brand X.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2124.38,
      "end": 2126.14,
      "text": "Just goes to prove that we have, I think,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2126.2,
      "end": 2128.44,
      "text": "the greatest musicians in the world in this country.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2129.7,
      "end": 2130.78,
      "text": "It's 22 minutes to 11.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2130.78,
      "end": 2133.5,
      "text": "and I'd like to say hello to a lovely young lady,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2133.66,
      "end": 2135.52,
      "text": "that is the description used by John Mead,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2135.64,
      "end": 2137.68,
      "text": "a lovely young lady by the name of Susie Scott.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2138.24,
      "end": 2139.82,
      "text": "Susie Scott has got to be told this,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2139.82,
      "end": 2142.34,
      "text": "that I was not wishing to be nosy, says John,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2142.6,
      "end": 2144.04,
      "text": "but just wanted to say good evening,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2144.22,
      "end": 2146.22,
      "text": "I think she's wonderful and I love her very much.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2146.66,
      "end": 2148.26,
      "text": "Oh, and by the way, says John,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2148.52,
      "end": 2152.44,
      "text": "he's the one in the Thin Lizzy 82 shirt, Susie.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2154.82,
      "end": 2156.82,
      "text": "Timmy Chan lives in Salford",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2156.82,
      "end": 2159.0,
      "text": "and he wants me to say hello to everybody who are,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2159.34,
      "end": 2160.28,
      "text": "everybody who is rather,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2160.28,
      "end": 2162.76,
      "text": "studying biochemistry in Salford University.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2165.15,
      "end": 2166.67,
      "text": "Little letter here from Debbie Inman,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2166.79,
      "end": 2169.71,
      "text": "who lives near Bishop, Auckland, in County Durham, says,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2170.74,
      "end": 2172.6,
      "text": "Here, Tom, say hello to Michael Mazzetti",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2172.6,
      "end": 2175.88,
      "text": "of Thistle Fiat Estate, I think it is, Croke County, Durham.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2176.26,
      "end": 2178.7,
      "text": "Also say hello to his mum and dad and brother Mark.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2179.02,
      "end": 2181.0,
      "text": "And finally, will I give Michael this message?",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2181.36,
      "end": 2183.6,
      "text": "Don't fret, your legs ain't that bad.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2183.6,
      "end": 2185.5,
      "text": "No one's made perfect.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2185.94,
      "end": 2187.12,
      "text": "I still love you very much.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2188.78,
      "end": 2191.02,
      "text": "He's got problems with his legs. You want to see mine?",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2191.02,
      "end": 2202.42,
      "text": "that's a track from a compilation album which has just come out on the ebony record label which is",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2340.0,
      "end": 2743.65,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 2743.65,
      "end": 2749.83,
      "text": "based in hull it's a track by a band called savage the album is called metal fatigue the track you",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2749.83,
      "end": 2756.99,
      "text": "heard had the title ain't no fit place and before that hot space is the title of the album from",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2756.99,
      "end": 2762.23,
      "text": "whence you heard the track called dancer it's by queen and it's from their new album out on emi",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2762.23,
      "end": 2767.95,
      "text": "it's 11 and a half minutes thereabouts to 11 o'clock i know that maurice michelson",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2767.95,
      "end": 2769.77,
      "text": "of 28 Time Bank,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2769.99,
      "end": 2772.07,
      "text": "when blatant time and wear is listening.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2772.45,
      "end": 2773.55,
      "text": "Maurice, wish you well.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2773.71,
      "end": 2775.83,
      "text": "Hope everything's, well, good for you.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2778.06,
      "end": 2781.0,
      "text": "Story here of a gentleman who's an honest fella.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2781.72,
      "end": 2784.6,
      "text": "Gave a fella a fiver yesterday for a two-pound cab ride.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2785.08,
      "end": 2786.62,
      "text": "And he didn't have any change, so I said,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2786.62,
      "end": 2788.94,
      "text": "well, drop the change into me at the BBC, and he did.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2789.44,
      "end": 2791.54,
      "text": "An honest fella. Wants me to say hello to his kids.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2791.68,
      "end": 2793.02,
      "text": "His kids are Jamie and Joanne.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2793.62,
      "end": 2795.92,
      "text": "Jamie and Joanne, your dad is an honest man.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2797.66,
      "end": 2798.4,
      "text": "And I thank him.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2801.07,
      "end": 2803.33,
      "text": "This is Gillen once again from our session by then.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2803.57,
      "end": 2805.55,
      "text": "It's called Haterly Bop Bop.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2805.71,
      "end": 2808.71,
      "text": "Ancient Mysteries.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3431.84,
      "end": 3434.12,
      "text": "And before that, Gillen and Haterly Bop Bop.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3434.58,
      "end": 3436.24,
      "text": "It's 11 o'clock, this is Radio 1,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3436.38,
      "end": 3437.92,
      "text": "and it's time for the Friday Night Connection.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3438.5,
      "end": 3440.24,
      "text": "Right, the tracks we played you last week were these.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3440.32,
      "end": 3443.24,
      "text": "Machine Gun from the album Wheels of Steel by Saxon.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3443.76,
      "end": 3446.3,
      "text": "Tomorrow Never Knows from Revolver by The Beatles.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3446.62,
      "end": 3449.24,
      "text": "And The Battle from Magnum 2 by Magnum.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3450.35,
      "end": 3452.05,
      "text": "Just about everybody got it right,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3452.05,
      "end": 3454.75,
      "text": "but we unfortunately can only afford 10 quid a week",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3454.75,
      "end": 3457.49,
      "text": "in the shape and form of a record token to give away as a prize.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3457.95,
      "end": 3459.79,
      "text": "And it's going to go this week to Mrs Sue Roberts",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3459.79,
      "end": 3463.43,
      "text": "of 18 Dundas Road, Peckham, London, SE15, Pride Be White.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3464.01,
      "end": 3464.77,
      "text": "Just around the corner.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3465.51,
      "end": 3467.51,
      "text": "Well done, Sue. The answer, of course, was guns.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3468.62,
      "end": 3472.1,
      "text": "Album Revolver, Machine Gun, tracked by Saxon, and Magnum.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3472.24,
      "end": 3474.46,
      "text": "That, of course, is one of those Clint Eastwood efforts.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3478.46,
      "end": 3480.5,
      "text": "Sue will also be sending you a Def Leppard T-shirt.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3480.6,
      "end": 3481.82,
      "text": "I've got it on in the studio now.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3481.86,
      "end": 3483.56,
      "text": "I promised to wash it before we ship it to you.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3487.07,
      "end": 3488.81,
      "text": "As everybody knows, part of the deal",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3488.81,
      "end": 3491.27,
      "text": "is to put together your own Friday Night Connection as well.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3491.43,
      "end": 3492.55,
      "text": "Sue put together quite a number.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3492.77,
      "end": 3494.07,
      "text": "This is the one that we chose.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3494.19,
      "end": 3496.51,
      "text": "Three bits of music, the connections contained therein.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3496.95,
      "end": 3498.41,
      "text": "Start listening now.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3498.73,
      "end": 3502.33,
      "text": "The Friday Night Connection for tonight,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4761.17,
      "end": 4764.55,
      "text": "put together by Mrs. Sue Roberts of 18 Dundas Road, Peckham, London.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4764.97,
      "end": 4767.53,
      "text": "Sue, I played as much of the theme one as I could for you there,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4767.57,
      "end": 4769.67,
      "text": "because I know you want to hear it one day in its entirety",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4769.67,
      "end": 4771.41,
      "text": "without me ravening over it,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4771.43,
      "end": 4773.09,
      "text": "but unfortunately I can't play it all tonight.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4773.51,
      "end": 4775.27,
      "text": "But I will do one night, especially for you.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4775.59,
      "end": 4775.95,
      "text": "Congratulations.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4776.47,
      "end": 4779.23,
      "text": "You get the £10 record token and the Def Leppard T-shirt as well.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4779.23,
      "end": 4783.95,
      "text": "now if anybody out there feels they know what the connection is jot it down on a postcard or",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4783.95,
      "end": 4789.01,
      "text": "any form of written communication you care to employ and send it to your answer that is",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4789.01,
      "end": 4797.55,
      "text": "the friday night connection the friday rock show bbc radio one london w1a 4ww friday night",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4797.55,
      "end": 4804.63,
      "text": "connection the friday rock show bbc radio one london w1a 4ww but please do it pretty quickly",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4804.63,
      "end": 4809.53,
      "text": "like tomorrow because next week's program is going to be pre-recorded because i will be in",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4809.53,
      "end": 4815.59,
      "text": "birmingham doing a live television broadcast on bbc one with status quo at that time so get those",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4815.59,
      "end": 4921.84,
      "text": "connections in as fast as you can good luck and here's more gillan you join me to another ball",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4921.84,
      "end": 4939.1,
      "text": "again until you've got a little wooden house you get a piece of land or just a patch of forest",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4939.1,
      "end": 4941.16,
      "text": "With your handsome meat",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4941.16,
      "end": 4943.94,
      "text": "So you can sit and eat",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4943.94,
      "end": 4946.54,
      "text": "When you're warm and fat",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4946.54,
      "end": 4949.78,
      "text": "You can go to bed",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4949.78,
      "end": 4978.22,
      "text": "Oh, yes, you will feel so good",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4978.22,
      "end": 4980.8,
      "text": "And she will share your life",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4980.8,
      "end": 4983.5,
      "text": "She'll calm your wife",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4983.5,
      "end": 4985.94,
      "text": "When you're warm and fat",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4985.94,
      "end": 4991.34,
      "text": "Recorded way back on the 26th of February, 1976.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6044.06,
      "end": 6045.76,
      "text": "That was Brand X out of the archives.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6045.94,
      "end": 6048.02,
      "text": "The track was called Kubil Blitz.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6050.27,
      "end": 6052.69,
      "text": "Brand X at that time were John Goodsell on guitar,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6052.91,
      "end": 6055.09,
      "text": "Rob Lumley on keyboards, Percy Jones on the bass,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6055.17,
      "end": 6056.27,
      "text": "and Phil Collins on the drums.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6056.73,
      "end": 6059.09,
      "text": "Good Genesis album coming out soon, a live one.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6060.11,
      "end": 6062.27,
      "text": "And before that, something from our session by Gillan,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6062.49,
      "end": 6065.61,
      "text": "a studio version of the track called Born to Kill.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6068.68,
      "end": 6071.52,
      "text": "It's 17 minutes to midnight. This is Alcatraz.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6072.0,
      "end": 6078.0,
      "text": "That's the new single, which is out by Iron Maiden",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6300.0,
      "end": 6544.7,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 6544.7,
      "end": 6546.7,
      "text": "from their recent number one album.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6546.86,
      "end": 6548.32,
      "text": "It's called The Number of the Beast.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6548.5,
      "end": 6550.9,
      "text": "And before that, something from a new album that's out on RCA",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6550.9,
      "end": 6552.86,
      "text": "by the band called Alcatraz.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6553.02,
      "end": 6555.06,
      "text": "The album is called Radio 5.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6555.56,
      "end": 6557.61,
      "text": "It was called Blame It On The Night.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6559.32,
      "end": 6561.64,
      "text": "And that was all played especially for Mark Bryant,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6561.8,
      "end": 6564.78,
      "text": "who's got a 20th birthday today, the 7th of May,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6565.02,
      "end": 6567.9,
      "text": "from Mrs. M. Presley of Plymouth and Devon.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6569.33,
      "end": 6572.23,
      "text": "And also for Graham, because he's got a 20th birthday",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6572.23,
      "end": 6573.51,
      "text": "coming up on the 12th of May.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6574.15,
      "end": 6576.77,
      "text": "Best wishes to him from Rick and Chunky and Stig and Pearson",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6576.77,
      "end": 6579.17,
      "text": "and everybody else that knows the fellow that wrote this.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6579.37,
      "end": 6581.91,
      "text": "And that fellow is Robert Douglas of Grimsby.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6582.69,
      "end": 6588.84,
      "text": "And here's a really old track.",
      "source": "TV"
    }
  ]
}